    283  f0ef							; --- E4 moth body (bank2 free space $F008-$F9D8) -------------------------
    284  f0ef							; Entered from bank0 via the $FEF0 entry tramp (sta $1FF8 lands on the
    285  f0ef							; jmp below at $FEF3). Exits via `jmp MothExitPad` ($FC49): bank2 runs
    286  f0ef							; sta $1FF6, bank0 serves jmp UE_Next. Rules:
    287  f0ef							;   - NEVER jsr FoldIndirect or any bank0 routine (a fold from inside
    288  f0ef							;     bank2 would switch away mid-routine = frozen player).
    289  f0ef							;   - Enemy records ARE here (org $F9D9) — read directly, no fold needed.
    290  f0ef							;   - Keep the whole routine inline (no jsr): tramps are tail jmps so
    291  f0ef							;     the stack depth equals the UE body (+0 vs the $F8 guard).
    292  f0ef							;   - ZP (rect cache, EnemyRam*, EnemyDataLo/Hi) is RAM: bank-independent.
    293  f100					      org	$F100
    294  f100				   MothRoutine
    295  f100							; E4 Stage C: horizontal patrol (docs/e4_moth_plan.md). 1 px / 2 frames
    296  f100							; (EnemyRamP & 1), range = spawn ± 8 tiles (32 px), wall/range/wrap =
    297  f100							; flip dir + hold, clear = commit candidate. Row/col inputs feed a
    298  f100							; verbatim copy of PlayerHitsMap's P3.4 rect walk; HIT turns instead of
    299  f100							; returning C=1.
    300  f100							; In: X = slot, Y = record base, FetchPtr = record base (records are in
    301  f100							; THIS bank — direct (FetchPtr),Y reads, NO fold). NEVER jsr bank0
    302  f100							; (mid-bank2 fold = frozen player). Slot is saved to EnemyIndex because
    303  f100							; the col swap and walk both use X (E3 lesson). Every exit re-stages
    304  f100							; FetchPtr (the walk overwrites it with window bytes) then
    305  f100							; jmp MothExitPad (sta $1FF6 / jmp UE_Next in bank0).
    306  f100		       a5 c2		      lda	EnemyRamP
    307  f102		       29 01		      and	#1
    308  f104		       f0 03		      beq	.MothRun	; branch-over-jmp (tail labels exceed ±127)
    309  f106		       4c 1a f2 	      jmp	MothExit	; ÷2 gate: 1 px / 2 frames
    310  f109				   .MothRun
    311  f109		       86 b9		      stx	EnemyIndex	; slot — turn/commit paths restore it
    312  f10b		       a5 c1		      lda	EnemyRamD	; live dir bit
    313  f10d		       3d 25 f2 	      and	MothBitTable,X
    314  f110		       d0 08		      bne	.MothR
    315  f112		       b5 bd		      lda	EnemyRamX,X
    316  f114		       38		      sec
    317  f115		       e9 01		      sbc	#1
    318  f117		       4c 1f f1 	      jmp	.MothChk
    319  f11a				   .MothR
    320  f11a		       b5 bd		      lda	EnemyRamX,X
    321  f11c		       18		      clc
    322  f11d		       69 01		      adc	#1
    323  f11f				   .MothChk
    324  f11f		       c9 a0		      cmp	#160
    325  f121		       90 03		      bcc	.MothChk2	; branch-over-jmp (tail labels exceed ±127)
    326  f123		       4c 11 f2 	      jmp	.MothTurn	; wrap (left edge) or off right edge -> turn.
